 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# UNNEST expression in BigQuery not handling array of structs correctly\n\nThe `_parse_unnest` method in the BigQuery dialect is not correctly handling array of structs when parsing UNNEST expressions. The current implementation has been simplified and is missing important functionality.\n\nWhen trying to run a query with UNNEST on an array of structs, I get errors. For example:\n\n```sql\nSELECT name, laps FROM UNNEST([STRUCT('Rudisha' AS name, [23.4, 26.3, 26.4, 26.1] AS laps), STRUCT('Makhloufi' AS name, [24.5, 25.4, 26.6, 26.1] AS laps)])\n```\n\nThis should work but fails because the current implementation doesn't properly handle the type annotations and exploding of nested array fields.\n\nThe issue is in the `_parse_unnest` method in `sqlglot/dialects/bigquery.py` which has been simplified and is missing the code that:\n1. Annotates types for the unnest expression\n2. Detects when unnesting a nested array (array of structs) and sets the `explode_array` flag\n\nTo reproduce:\n1. Run a query that uses UNNEST with an array of structs\n2. Observe that it fails with type errors\n\nThis affects any query that uses UNNEST with complex nested data structures in BigQuery.\n</issue>\n",
